    "abstract": null,
    "field": "Land-use effects on climate",
    "problem": "Existing methods for quantifying the climatic impact of urbanization are unreliable, as comparing urban versus rural observations yields significantly different warming estimates depending on whether areas are classified by population data or satellite-measured night lights.",
    "method": "To estimate the impact of land-use changes on surface warming, the authors propose using the difference between trends in observed surface temperatures and corresponding trends from a global weather reanalysis that is insensitive to local surface effects such as urbanization.",
    "task": "The task is to estimate the impact of urbanization and other land-use changes on surface temperature warming by comparing observed temperature trends with those from a global reanalysis dataset that is insensitive to these local surface effects.",
